<title>USA: Worthington Industries buys panel maker.</title>
<headline>Worthington Industries buys panel maker.</headline>
<dateline>COLUMBUS, Ohio 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Worthington Industries Inc said on Monday it has signed a definitive agreement to buy Gerstenslager Co, an automotive body panel maker, in a stock-for-stock exchange valued at $113 million.</p>
<p>Gerstenslager is owned by JMAC, an investment company controlled by Worthington's chairman emeritus, John McConnell.</p>
<p>Gerstenslager has more than 1,000 employees and annual sales of $120 million.</p>
</text>
